heading("Appendix B", "Reproduction Checklist")
para(
    "Data: Fashion-MNIST via torchvision, auto-downloaded; splits built by models/data.py with seed 42 "
    "(Table V). Code: models/autoencoders.py, scripts/train.py, scripts/evaluate.py, scripts/figures.py, "
    "scripts/run_all.sh. Checkpoints: five .pt files with per-run metrics JSON and per-image error arrays. "
    "Figures: generated by scripts/figures.py from the saved errors; no hand editing. Randomness: seed 42 "
    "controls initialization, shuffling, subset sampling, and noise. Compute: two-core CPU, \u224810 minutes "
    "total. All artifacts needed to reproduce every table and figure are retained with the project."
)

heading("Appendix C", "Metric Computation Details")
para(
    "All metrics are computed with scikit-learn on the 10,000-image test set (9,000 normal, 1,000 anomalies). "
    "The threshold \u03c4 is numpy.percentile of the 2,000 normal validation errors at the chosen percentile. "
    "Precision, recall, and F1 come from precision_recall_fscore_support on binary predictions s(x) > \u03c4. "
    "ROC-AUC is roc_auc_score and PR-AUC is average_precision_score, both evaluated on the raw scores s(x) "
    "with anomaly as the positive class. No tie-breaking is needed: per-image MSE values are effectively "
    "continuous. The scripts record every metric, the threshold, and the per-image error arrays to JSON/NPZ "
    "files alongside each checkpoint, so Tables IX, XI, and XIV can be recomputed without retraining."
)

